<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">witch</ansi>

The Witch is a control caster. It deals almost no damage; it takes the
enemy's turns away instead. Its hexes put foes to sleep, paralyze them,
knock them down, slow them, poison them, and leave them open to the
company's blows, and each hex reaches more foes as the Witch levels. A
company with a Witch fights fewer enemy turns than it takes.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What the Witch is</ansi>

  Health      1 to start, 0.55 a level to level 20 (<ansi fg="command">help health</ansi>)
  Skill       Attack 0.7 and Evasion 0.75 a level, like a wizard (<ansi fg="command">help evasion</ansi>)
  Gear        light armor, no shield, any weapon (<ansi fg="command">help armor</ansi>)
  Mana        40 and 10 a level, refilled only by a rest, an inn or a draught
              (<ansi fg="command">help mana</ansi>)
  Stats       mysticism 4, smarts 3, perception 2, vitality 1 (<ansi fg="command">help growth</ansi>)
  Starts with Slumber, and Withering Hex, a weak damage curse. Earthbind
              comes at level 3, and the rest by level 18 (<ansi fg="command">help hexes</ansi>).
  Starter kit an ash quarterstaff, a leather cap, a cotton shirt, a student's
              amulet, food, a waterskin, a minor mana draught and a knapsack
  Utility     Weather Sense (<ansi fg="command">help forecast</ansi>)

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How a Witch fights</ansi>

A Witch's strategy role is <ansi fg="command">controller</ansi> (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>). In a battle it hexes on its
own, with no command from you. Each round it picks the first hex it knows
that has a foe worth it: a foe not already under that hex, not shaking off
a recent one, and (for Blight) a healer. It aims first at a foe winding up a
heavy blow, then a caster that is chanting, then the nearest foe. When no hex
has a foe left to take, it casts Withering Hex, and when it has no mana, it
swings.

Hexes are real casts. They cost mana, take chanting rounds, and a blow that
draws blood on the Witch may break the chant (<ansi fg="command">help interrupts</ansi>), so keep it
behind the front. A foe can resist a hex (<ansi fg="command">help hexes</ansi>); the Witch is told so.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Other Witches</ansi>

A Witch companion hexes the same way. Recruits are hired like any other
(<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>); two Witches never hex the same foe at once. A company
of fighters and one Witch fights best when the Witch's hexes take the foes
the fighters are about to face.

At level 10 a Witch promotes to a Hedge Witch, Coven Sage or Hag (<ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>).

Commands: <ansi fg="command">archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">strategy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">spells</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help hexes</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help hexes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
